# tinybendygrad/runtime/__init__.bend -- port of tinygrad/runtime/__init__.py
#
# `tinygrad/runtime/__init__.py` is ZERO BYTES. Same finding as
# `mixin/__init__.py`: an empty upstream that exists only to mark a
# package boundary, no re-exports, no names. Submodule imports resolve
# by path in Bend the same way Python's do by name, so this file holds
# the boundary and nothing else.
